  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": "Dissolve ingredients (except bicarbonate, vitamins, cysteine and sulfide), sparge medium with 80% H2 and 20% CO2 gas mixture for 30 - 45 min to make it anoxic."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "Add and dissolve bicarbonate and adjust pH to 6.5, then dispense medium under 80% H2 and 20% CO2 gas atmosphere into anoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials to 30% of their volume and autoclave."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": "After sterilization add cysteine and sulfide from sterile anoxic stock solutions autoclaved under 100% N2 gas."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": "Vitamins are prepared under 100% N2 gas atmosphere and sterilized by filtration."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": "Adjust pH of complete medium to 6.8 - 7.0, if necessary."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": "2. For incubation use sterile 80% H2 and 20% CO2 gas mixture at two atmospheres of pressure."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": "3. Note: If the medium is being used without overpressure then adjust pH with a small amount of sterile anoxic 1 N HCl, if necessary."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 11,
      "comment": "First dissolve nitrilotriacetic acid and adjust pH to 6.5 with KOH, then add minerals. Adjust final to pH 7.0 with KOH."
    },
